              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Fluctuating job demands are part of the construction and hauling business. One month you're stretched thin, the next you're watching overhead eat into margins. For many owner-operators and small fleets, finding ways to stay flexible without overspending is key, and that's where searching for a used dump trailer for sale can make a real difference.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we work with contractors and haulers every day who want to grow responsibly. Purchasing a used dump trailer is one of the most practical ways to expand capacity, control costs, and protect long-term profitability without taking on unnecessary financial risk.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-financial-sense",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Used Dump Trailers Make Financial Sense",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "financial-sense"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-financial-sense-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "New equipment is appealing, but it can come with higher upfront costs, longer lead times, and early depreciation. A used dump trailer, when properly inspected and sourced from a reputable dealer, delivers the same core functionality at a significantly lower price point. Trailers can lose value within the first few years while still having many productive years left. Buying used allows you to avoid that initial depreciation while still putting dependable equipment to work. For owner-operators focused on cash flow and long-term planning, that matters.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-financial-sense-2-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "styles": {
